 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? Bear resistant box above the stove is the clear winner. Keeps your gear from getting wet too. Most bears live far beyond night vision, so ten feet or so is enough. Keep it high enough a dog can't reach, like fifteen. Make noise with a horn or bell, and leave the food inside. Bears associate a tent with danger and leave. The box works too, you just need to leave food on the platform.",
